# Build-context exclusions for Containerfile.
#
# The context is a fresh clone made by the image-build rail's initContainer, so
# this is not primarily about size -- it is about CORRECTNESS. Two entries are
# load-bearing:
#
#   dist/          a stale binary from a developer's local `bun run build`
#                  would be copied in and then overwritten by the build stage.
#                  Harmless today, but it makes the image depend on the state
#                  of whoever's checkout produced the context.
#   node_modules/  a host-installed tree can carry platform-native binaries
#                  built for macOS. `bun install --frozen-lockfile` runs in the
#                  image and must be what populates this.
#
# The rest is noise that has no business in a build context.

dist/
node_modules/
.git/
.github/
.forgejo/
_archive/
.qmd/
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
.env
.env.*
